{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers","id":1131980,"title":"Why didn't the Tribes help the White Howlers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-20T18:22:36-07:00","id":1131980,"title":"Why didn't the Tribes help the White Howlers?","content":"Was it ever explained why the Garou never came to the White Howlers aid? It REALLY seems hard to believe, though it does add to the tragedy of the whole story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:35:33-07:00","id":1131983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers#post1131980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it ever explained why the Garou never came to the White Howlers aid? It REALLY seems hard to believe, though it does add to the tragedy of the whole story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's a lot of convoluted reasons but the short answer is the Garou generally hate each other and have only recently come to any form of union.<br /> <br /> Also, by the time there was something to do about the staggeringly stupid decision of the WH, it was too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:35:43-07:00","id":1131984,"title":"","content":"Can't seem to locate which of my books says it (or my White Howler Tribebook mysteriously vanished) but:<br /> <br /> I think it was a combination of the rest of the Garou Nation didn't believe them when they said they found a path into Malfeas, those that did believe them thought it had to have been a trap, or they thought it was suicide and wasn't going to go.<br /> <br /> Presumably the other Tribes didn't think the Howlers would be crazy enough to throw their entire Tribe and didn't try to warn them away as well as they should have, but there you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:40:01-07:00","id":1131987,"title":"","content":"In short, it was a plan so stupid you'd think the Silver Fangs would be involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:45:32-07:00","id":1131990,"title":"","content":"The back of the book gives a long list of reasons where either they Howlers weren't believed, were too far away (Pure Lands and Australia), culturally aligned with the Romans (Warders of Men), or were having Roman problems of their own and couldn't really spare aide (Fianna).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:49:50-07:00","id":1132007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1131990#post1131990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The back of the book gives a long list of reasons where either they Howlers weren't believed, were too far away (Pure Lands and Australia), culturally aligned with the Romans (Warders of Men), or were having Roman problems of their own and couldn't really spare aide (Fianna).</div> </div> </div> </div>A sizable body of Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs were also aligned with the Romans. The Garou Nation really seemed to go astray during the Pax Romana...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:04:35-07:00","id":1132013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1132007#post1132007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A sizable body of Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs were also aligned with the Romans. The Garou Nation really seemed to go astray during the Pax Romana...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remembered the Warders, and I wanted to say the Fangs and Lords, but I wasn't certain enough (and didn't have my book on me to verify). That section of the book helped save the new reason for the Howler's fall for me because I thought the idea of the Garou not showing up to help was weird. Especially the Fianna, I know they aren't the most popular tribe on this forums (from being on here it seems like the least) but a lot of the lore (Tribe books, Dark Ages, ect.) really made it seem like the two tribes were close. To have the Fianna not show up seemed out of character (but when you explain they just don't have Garou to send/lend it becomes more sensible). <br /> <br /> I can actually see the Fianna not sending Garou to help the Howlers due to the Celtic lack of unity and thinking on a local scale combined with dealing with the Romans and the supernatural threats they carried with them (the same issues the Howlers themselves were dealing with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 08-20-2017, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T00:14:52-07:00","id":1132111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1132013#post1132013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I remembered the Warders, and I wanted to say the Fangs and Lords, but I wasn't certain enough (and didn't have my book on me to verify). That section of the book helped save the new reason for the Howler's fall for me because I thought the idea of the Garou not showing up to help was weird. Especially the Fianna, I know they aren't the most popular tribe on this forums (from being on here it seems like the least) but a lot of the lore (Tribe books, Dark Ages, ect.) really made it seem like the two tribes were close. To have the Fianna not show up seemed out of character (but when you explain they just don't have Garou to send/lend it becomes more sensible).<br /> <br /> I can actually see the Fianna not sending Garou to help the Howlers due to the Celtic lack of unity and thinking on a local scale combined with dealing with the Romans and the supernatural threats they carried with them (the same issues the Howlers themselves were dealing with).</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, the Howlers were at that point pretty much done for anyway. Their kinfolk and their spirit allies corrupted to the scale it basically doomed the tribe. Had they had the time, no doubt they would have managed to gather some allies. But they didn't and so they had to act in the moment the best they could.<br /> <br /> Does not excuse the rest ignoring their pleas, but explains why the Howlers still went down the tunnel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T02:11:39-07:00","id":1132128,"title":"","content":"The story of the White Howlers is usually offered as a reminder of the danger posed by pride. Did they even look for help, to begin with?<br /> Since at that point the garou tribes were a bit more divided than in the present day, especially the ones strongly rooted in the human society, it maybe made sense for a Pict-oriented tribe to act alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T03:19:07-07:00","id":1132146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1132128#post1132128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story of the White Howlers is usually offered as a reminder of the danger posed by pride. Did they even look for help, to begin with?<br /> Since at that point the garou tribes were a bit more divided than in the present day, especially the ones strongly rooted in the human society, it maybe made sense for a Pict-oriented tribe to act alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did as of the latest version of their fall, in the Howler Tribebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:53:04-07:00","id":1132195,"title":"","content":"Cuz Garou was hypocritical assholes as usually?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:01:12-07:00","id":1132252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1132013#post1132013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remembered the Warders, and I wanted to say the Fangs and Lords, but I wasn't certain enough (and didn't have my book on me to verify). That section of the book helped save the new reason for the Howler's fall for me because I thought the idea of the Garou not showing up to help was weird. Especially the Fianna, I know they aren't the most popular tribe on this forums (from being on here it seems like the least) but a lot of the lore (Tribe books, Dark Ages, ect.) really made it seem like the two tribes were close. To have the Fianna not show up seemed out of character (but when you explain they just don't have Garou to send/lend it becomes more sensible).<br /> <br /> I can actually see the Fianna not sending Garou to help the Howlers due to the Celtic lack of unity and thinking on a local scale combined with dealing with the Romans and the supernatural threats they carried with them (the same issues the Howlers themselves were dealing with).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why the Fianna seem to be so unpopular on these forums (I get the same impression, actually), but their reasons for not helping the White Howlers are probably different from the reasons some of the other tribes didn't help. It may have come down to the White Howlers being in a more desperate situation than anyone else was willing to believe on short notice, but given a little more time, the Fianna and some others might have been willing to come to their aid, if for no other motive than to offer counsel against self-destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T14:04:08-07:00","id":1132793,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, in the older editions the White Howlers didn't even ask for help. They charged in there to fight the Wyrm on their own out of pride and hubris and the other Tribes didn't even really know what happened until after the fact. In the newer accounts though the White Howlers did ask for help but nobody bothered to respond. Personally I tend to prefer the older accounts because I think it serves as a good warning about chasing after the Wyrm half-cocked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T14:09:38-07:00","id":1132797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1132793#post1132793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally I tend to prefer the older accounts because I think it serves as a good warning about chasing after the Wyrm half-cocked.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> MY THOUGHTS SINCE BOOK OF THE WYRM 20 CAME OUT!!! Man I talked about it a bit back then on here and felt alone in my opinion. I liked that each of the lost tribes represented a different lesson for the Garou. The new version of the White Howlers veers into Croatan territory of taking on too much on your own. The Croatan knew did what they did knowing they were going to die, and thought they were saving everyone else, which implies if responsibility was shared, maybe the Croatan would still be around. The Holwers were convinced they were nasty enough to go in and win alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T17:14:01-07:00","id":1133218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers#post1131980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it ever explained why the Garou never came to the White Howlers aid? It REALLY seems hard to believe, though it does add to the tragedy of the whole story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems no less believable than ACTIVELY ATTACKING your fellow chosen of Gaia. Garou are dicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T17:29:52-07:00","id":1133223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1133218#post1133218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems no less believable than ACTIVELY ATTACKING your fellow chosen of Gaia. Garou are dicks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree as its action vs inaction. Garou actively killing Fera, each other, slaughtering the Bunyip, that's all being too eager to enter combat. Staying away is the opposite of that and why it was a little hard to swallow. The back of the book helped but I still wasn't a fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T19:48:54-07:00","id":1133263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1133223#post1133223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I disagree as its action vs inaction. Garou actively killing Fera, each other, slaughtering the Bunyip, that's all being too eager to enter combat. Staying away is the opposite of that and why it was a little hard to swallow. The back of the book helped but I still wasn't a fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou are litterally the most divided and fractous of changing breeds. The idea that &quot;You aren't my tribe fuck off&quot; seems pretty reasonable to me especially at the &quot;height&quot; of their power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T06:41:46-07:00","id":1133348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1133218#post1133218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems no less believable than ACTIVELY ATTACKING your fellow chosen of Gaia. Garou are dicks.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember it right, the Garou king of the time was suffering from the Curse of the Silver Fangs and therefore extra paranoid. The relationships between shapechangers were already cold enough because of Ananasi deceptions (who lied to the Garou to make them free their queen from Malfeas), Gurhal reticence (who refused to share the secret of returning people to life) and other slights I don't really remember anymore; so, when one of the Silver Fangs packs disappeared in Fera territory, the mad king blamed the Fera and many garou were glad to slay them as payback, while many others obeyed out of simple loyalty to the Litany and their king.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 08-24-2017, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T14:38:32-07:00","id":1133552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1131980-why-didn-t-the-tribes-help-the-white-howlers?p=1133223#post1133223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I disagree as its action vs inaction. Garou actively killing Fera, each other, slaughtering the Bunyip, that's all being too eager to enter combat. Staying away is the opposite of that and why it was a little hard to swallow. The back of the book helped but I still wasn't a fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still trying to wrap my head any Garou was stupid enough for the plan of INVADING HELL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T15:59:23-07:00","id":1133573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"